 ],
 "literal": "In the small settlement near the hill where clouds play, / as the milch cows hasten towards their calves, in the forest pasture, / the green-leaved jasmine's blemishless white flowers / have assumed the beauty of the red sky. / I will not survive, it seems, O friend, I indeed!",
 "translation": "O friend, I do not think I will survive. In the small settlement near the hill where clouds play, the milch cows have hastened back to their calves. In the forest pasture, the blemishless white flowers of the green-leaved jasmine have assumed the beauty of the red twilight sky.",
 "modern": "மேகங்கள் விளையாடும் மலைக்கு அருகில் உள்ள சிறிய குடியிருப்புக்கு, கறவை மாடுகள் தம் கன்றுகளை நோக்கிச் செல்ல, முல்லை நிலத்துக் காட்டில், பசிய இலைகளைக் கொண்ட முல்லையின் குற்றமற்ற வெண்மையான மலர்கள், செவ்வானத்தின் அழகைப் பெற்றுள்ளன. தோழியே! நான் உயிர் பிழைக்க மாட்டேன் என்று தோன்றுகிறது.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her confidante during the mullai (forest) season, which is the time of the hero's promised return. She points out the signs of evening: the clouds playing on the hills, the milch cows rushing back to their calves in the small hamlet, and the pure white jasmine flowers blooming in the forest pasture, looking like stars against the red twilight sky. These sights of homecoming and evening intensify her grief of separation, making her feel that she cannot survive without her lover. The imagery of the cows returning to their calves contrasts with her own state of loneliness, highlighting her yearning. Key words include 'முல்லை' (jasmine/forest region), 'கறவை' (milch cow), 'செவ்வான்' (red sky), and 'உய்யேன்' (I will not survive).",
